  },
  {
   "type": "cols",
   "layout": "33-66",
   "columns": [
    [
     {
      "type": "textmedia",
      "header": "<h1> FAQ </h1>",
      "body": "<p>Frequently Asked Questions</p>",
      "images": [],
      "videos": [],
      "pos": "text",
      "cols": 1,
      "valign": "top",
      "ftype": "text",
      "id": "c1799",
      "bg": "",
      "space": {
       "before": "default",
       "after": "default"
      }
     }
    ],
    [
     {
      "type": "accordion",
      "header": "",
      "items": [
       {
        "title": "Why are there different camera models?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Depending on the tool dimensions and types to be inspected, ZOLLER offers three different camera technologies for »pomBasic«. This ensures that every customer receives a solution that is optimally tailored to their requirements.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1796",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Are the devices user-friendly?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Yes, in addition to its many other advantages, »pomBasic« stands out for its high level of user-friendliness. For example, the most important and frequently used functions can be organized into favorite groups. This ensures that all operators have quick and simple access to the required measurement functions.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1794",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Does »pomBasic« offer the option to enlarge cross-sectional images using digital zoom?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>A digital zoom is available in the control software for all camera models. Additionally, the »pomColorCam« and »pomMicroCam« models feature an optical zoom.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1792",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Are DXF comparisons supported on all devices in the »pomBasic« series?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The DXF function allows tools to be quickly and reliably optically aligned with their nominal contour in DXF format.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1790",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Are there options to quickly adjust the illumination settings for incident light and transmitted light?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>For incident light, an automatic illumination setting function is available at the touch of a button. Additionally, the quick-access function allows you to quickly and simply optimize all available illumination settings.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1788",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "When should I use a standard camera (»pomBasic«) or a micro camera (»pomBasic MTI«)?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Ideally, the diameter range for »the« »pomBasic« starts at 3 mm and increases toward the top. For the »pomBasic MTI«,« the diameter range starts as low as 0.2 mm and also increases toward the top.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1786",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Can »pomBasic MTI« also be used to measure larger tool diameters?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>The travel paths of the X-axis and Y-axis are identical for both device models. This allows even larger tool diameters to be reliably measured with the »pomBasic MTI«.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1784",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Does ZOLLER offer tool holders for »pomBasic« and »pomBasic MTI«?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>A wide variety of tool holders are available for a wide range of tool applications.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1782",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Why is there a CN control for the camera axis?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Enables combined focus on the tool, automatic camera positioning relative to the tool surface, and CNC-controlled movement of the camera axis via joystick.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1803",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       },
       {
        "title": "Why does the »pomBasic« MTI« camera have coaxial lighting, and what is it?",
        "blocks": [
         {
          "type": "textmedia",
          "header": "",
          "body": "<p>Coaxial illumination is integrated directly into the camera system and ensures optimal, shadow-free lighting of the tool surface, particularly for microtools.</p>",
          "images": [],
          "videos": [],
          "pos": "text",
          "cols": 1,
          "valign": "top",
          "ftype": "text",
          "id": "c1811",
          "bg": "",
          "space": {
           "before": "default",
           "after": "default"
          }
         }
        ]
       }
      ],
      "ftype": "accordion",
      "id": "c1798",
      "bg": "",
      "space": {
       "before": "default",
       "after": "default"
      }
     }
    ]
   ],
